<h1>Schedule</h1>
<%- if @message -%>
<%= notice(@message, kind: flash_kind(@message), dismiss: "/schedule") %>
<%- end -%>
<%- if @plan.empty? -%>
<p class="muted">No schedule configured — set one below (or set <span class="mono">schedule:</span>
in your config / run <span class="mono">pgkeeper connect</span>), then a
<span class="mono">maintenance:</span> block to schedule verify and prune too.</p>
<%- else -%>
<table>
  <tr><th>Job</th><th>Scope</th><th>Schedule</th><th>Cron</th><th>Next runs (UTC)</th><th>Run</th></tr>
  <%- @plan.each do |row| -%>
  <tr>
    <td>
      <%= pill(row.action, "") %>
      <%- unless row.flags.empty? -%><span class="mono muted"><%= h(row.flags.join(' ')) %></span><%- end -%>
    </td>
    <td><%= h(row.scope) %></td>
    <td><%= h(row.cadence) %></td>
    <td class="mono"><%= h(row.cron) %></td>
    <td>
      <%- if row.next_runs.empty? -%>
      <span class="muted">—</span>
      <%- else -%>
      <%- row.next_runs.each do |t| -%>
      <div class="mono"><%= h(fmt_time(t)) %></div>
      <%- end -%>
      <%- end -%>
    </td>
    <td>
      <%- danger = row.action == "prune" && row.flags.include?("--apply") -%>
      <form class="run-now" method="post" action="/actions/<%= u(row.action) %>"
            onsubmit="return pgkConfirm(this, 'Run <%= h(([row.action] + row.flags).join(' ')) %> now?')">
        <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= h(@csrf_token) %>">
        <%- if row.action == "backup" && row.only && row.only.length == 1 -%>
        <input type="hidden" name="database" value="<%= h(row.only.first) %>">
        <%- end -%>
        <%- if row.action == "verify" && row.flags.include?("--deep") -%>
        <input type="hidden" name="deep" value="on">
        <%- end -%>
        <%- if row.action == "prune" && row.flags.include?("--apply") -%>
        <input type="hidden" name="apply" value="on">
        <%- end -%>
        <button type="submit" class="btn-run<%= danger ? ' danger' : '' %>">Run now</button>
      </form>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <%- end -%>
</table>
<p class="muted">This is the plan resolved from your config — the same one
<span class="mono">pgkeeper schedule print</span> shows. It only fires on time once it's wired up:
<span class="mono">pgkeeper schedule install</span> (crontab lines) or
<span class="mono">--systemd</span> (timer units), or <span class="mono">pgkeeper daemon</span>
in a container. <strong>Run now</strong> triggers a job immediately through the same lock as a
scheduled run — never a second concurrent pipeline — and lands you on the
<a href="/actions">actions</a> page to watch it.</p>
<%- end -%>

<h2>Set a schedule</h2>
<%- if @editable -%>
<form class="action-card" method="post" action="/schedule/set">
  <div class="action-head">
    <span class="action-icon accent">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 7v5l3 3"/>
      </svg>
    </span>
    <div>
      <h3>Write to <span class="mono"><%= h(@config_path) %></span></h3>
      <p>Pick a database to give it its own cadence (overriding the global default), or edit the
      global default itself. The expression is validated first and the whole file is re-checked
      before the atomic write — comments and <span class="mono">ENV</span> interpolations survive.
      Leave the expression blank to remove an override. PgKeeper reads config at startup, so
      restart it (and re-run <span class="mono">pgkeeper schedule install</span> if you use
      cron/systemd) after saving.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= h(@csrf_token) %>">
  <div class="form-grid">
    <div class="field">
      <label class="field-label" for="sched-database">Scope</label>
      <select id="sched-database" name="database">
        <option value="">Global default<%= @global_schedule ? " — currently: #{h(@global_schedule)}" : " — none set" %></option>
        <%- @databases.each do |db| -%>
        <option value="<%= h(db.name) %>"><%= h(db.name) %><%= db.schedule ? " — currently: #{h(db.schedule)}" : " — inherits the global default" %></option>
        <%- end -%>
      </select>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label class="field-label" for="sched-expression">Schedule <span class="muted">— cron, natural language, or a shorthand; blank removes</span></label>
      <input type="text" id="sched-expression" name="expression"
             placeholder='0 13 * * * &#183; daily at 03:15 &#183; every monday at 9am &#183; hourly'>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="action-foot">
    <label class="switch"><input type="checkbox" name="confirm"><span class="slider"></span><span class="switch-label">Confirm</span></label>
    <button type="submit">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
      Save schedule
    </button>
  </div>
</form>
<%- else -%>
<p class="muted">Editing from the web is disabled: the loaded config
(<span class="mono"><%= h(@config_path) %></span>) is not an editable file from this process.
Set <span class="mono">schedule:</span> by editing the file directly.</p>
<%- end -%>
